{'vulnerability_type': 'Business Logic Flaw — Flash-Loan Amplified Ownership Check Bypass in Airdrop Claim', 'faulty_functions': [{'function_name': 'claimTokens()', 'trigger_point': {'transaction_hash': '0xeb8c3bebed11e2e4fcd30cbfc2fb3c55c4ca166003c7f7d319e78eaab9747098', 'index': 49017}, 'fault_description': 'The claimTokens() function determines airdrop eligibility solely based on current NFT ownership at call time (alpha.balanceOf(msg.sender) / beta.balanceOf(msg.sender)). It has NO protection against flash-loan-based temporary NFT ownership. An attacker can: (1) flash-loan BAYC-F tokens from NFTX vault, (2) redeem them for actual BAYC NFTs inside the flash loan callback, (3) call claimTokens() while temporarily holding the NFTs, (4) re-mint the NFTs back to repay the flash loan, and (5) walk away with the APE airdrop. The alphaClaimed[tokenId] mapping only prevents double-claiming per NFT ID but does not prevent a contract from temporarily acquiring unclaimed NFTs and claiming them within a single atomic transaction.', 'fix_strategy': 'Add a tx.origin == msg.sender check at the beginning of claimTokens() to prevent smart contracts (including flash-loan callbacks) from calling the function. This ensures only Externally Owned Accounts (EOAs) can claim the airdrop directly, blocking flash-loan-based attacks. Additionally, this preserves legitimate use cases where individual NFT holders manually claim. For a more comprehensive solution, consider implementing a snapshot-based Merkle proof system instead of on-chain balance enumeration.', 'core_patch_snippet': '// ... existing code ...\n\nfunction claimTokens() external whenNotPaused {\n+   // Prevent contract-based flash loan attacks: only EOAs can claim directly\n+   require(tx.origin == msg.sender, "AirdropGrapesToken: contracts cannot claim");\n    \n    require(block.timestamp >= claimStartTime && block.timestamp < claimStartTime + claimDuration, "Claimable period is finished");\n    require((beta.balanceOf(msg.sender) > 0 || alpha.balanceOf(msg.sender) > 0), "Nothing to claim");\n\n    // ... rest of existing logic unchanged ...\n}'}]}
</Fix_Strategy>

